[{:db/id -1 :doc/id "business-openrouter-b70-overload-resolution-20260908" :doc/title "Murakumo fixed-node overload resolution" :doc/as-of "2026-09-08" :source/dataset "business" :doc/body "# Fixed b70 overload classification: measured, corrected, deployed\n\nThe Slow, but cheap concept requires honest capacity signals. At 2026-09-08T07:59:12.676Z two public streaming requests occupied both live b70 slots. A third request returned HTTP 503 initializing-or-saturated in 59 ms without Retry-After. Both streams completed in about 38.7 seconds and the node returned idle. The fixed-node route incorrectly used RunPod cold-start admission.\n\nAPI PR https://github.com/network-awai/cloud-murakumo-api/pull/239 merged as 969928a9e297303f77b5162473bcbc0d020d9009. A fixed-node admission function now requires verified healthy model capacity: full slots return 429 all-slots-busy; missing health or wrong model return 503 node-unavailable. This also removes inappropriate cold-start admission for a stopped owned node.\n\nBuilt-worker HTTP tests cover saturation, unhealthy origin and wrong checkpoint, including exact reason and Retry-After. All three fail against the previous deployed bundle and pass against the rebuilt bundle. Pure readiness: 18 tests, 137 assertions. Native tests: 3 pass. Origin proxy: 4 pass. Two existing chat_fallback_timeout source-regex tests fail identically on old main and this patch, checking obsolete context/pool literals; they are not reported as green.\n\nDeployed Worker version 2b9cefac-d966-42e4-aea2-08083f2cdb91. Source digest d3c0f57589ac6587448b70187cf929a4bc15d00b59406c761046366f2381fee0. Worker SHA256 46f33a2d4c296b1b7682f15822893594c671526bf2c54bc7f0592b4be107f195. Root pin update b03d409c5d2220616fe32c6e9d04a7a6982b50d6.\n\nRepeat public experiment at 2026-09-08T08:06:50.497Z: two 13k-filler streaming requests occupied both slots. Third request returned 429 all-slots-busy with Retry-After: 5 in 45 ms. Both streams completed with HTTP 200 and DONE in 36.036 / 36.187 seconds. Both slots subsequently idle. A fresh exact-marker request returned 200 with correct content, fixed model and consistent positive usage in 6.853 seconds.\n\nThis closes one bounded live saturation / retry-header / subsequent-success test, not sustained capacity, reservation, atomic admission under simultaneous arrivals, cancellation propagation, backend restart recovery or model quality of the synthetic long streams. No customer content was captured. The independent seven-day marker ledger was not populated with these load requests. Catalog remains is_ready=false; application remains unsubmitted.\n\nLocal evidence hashes:\noverload.json SHA256 4ea3c00eb46b396f456510aee896917196022d5e6bba995020331fb253dde8e1\noverload-recovery.json SHA256 91785c491eb2ed04aed575f53ad37c548f929882b0eaa5037290b4e20c95409e\noverload-postfix.json SHA256 12148a8e2feb6f0f5533428b1672cdb1726bc96a77dedf9c598295d9dd867fb5\nstream-cancel.json SHA256 49841b560cb7f1149ec0d2a22c9fbb058a8e8261daebcba30ef8e3fb78dfd3f8\n"}]
